                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_217">Ford, Devon,
                                Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the
                                Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card records the following context for the rejection:
                                "There is no medieval indication of provenance. The book is in XIX
                                c. binding. Notes at front by <persName role="fmo">W.
                                    Maskell</persName> say 'I purchased this book at the Ford Abbey
                                sale, in 1846. This, with one other MS., a copy of part of S.
                                Augustin on the Psalms, was the only remnant of the ancient library
                                &amp; service books. The last leaf has unhappily lost its lower
                                portion: upon which, I doubt not, was written the usual 'Anathema.'"
                                On the index card, there are two additional notes in other hands.
                                The first indicates that the copy of St Augustine on the Psalms is
                                now at Chicago, Newberry Library, but probably not at Ford between
                                the dissolution and 1746. The second note highlights that the Ford
                                cartulary was bought by <persName>Mr Gwyn</persName>; see Hearne,
                                    <title>Collectanea</title> VIII, 160.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Ford Abbey sale 1846.</provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Purchased of the <persName role="fmo"
                                >Rev. Wm Maskell</persName> 3rd July 1847.'</provenance>
                    </history>
